lesson: 112
title: Speed: how far in so many hours
stars: 0
explain: Speed tells how far something goes in one hour: a car going 60 km each hour has a speed of 60 km an hour.
explain: Distance = speed × hours: in 3 hours that car goes 60 × 3 = 180 km.
explain: If you know the distance for some hours, divide to get the speed: 120 km in 2 hours is 120 / 2 = 60 km each hour.
explain: Going the other way, hours = distance / speed: 240 km at 60 km an hour takes 240 / 60 = 4 hours.
vars: a=name s=20..90 h=2..9 g=2..5
need: s * h <= 600
need: g != h
answer: s * h
exercise: A car goes {s} km each hour. How many km does it go in {h} hours?
exercise: {a}'s family drives at {s} km an hour. How far do they drive in {h} hours?
exercise: A train travels {s*g} km in {g} hours. At the same speed, how far does it travel in {h} hours?
exercise: A bus drives {s} km in one hour. How many km does it drive in {h} hours at that speed?
exercise: A boat sails {s*g} km in {g} hours. How many km does it sail in {h} hours if its speed stays the same?
exercise: A truck goes {s} km every hour. How far will it go in {h} hours?
test: How far does a van go in {h} hours when its speed is {s} km an hour?
test: In {g} hours a lorry covered {s*g} km. Keeping the same pace, what distance does it cover in {h} hours?
test: The speed of a ship is {s} km per hour. It sails for {h} hours. How many km is that?
test: {a} drove for {g} hours and went {s*g} km. Tomorrow {a.he} will drive {h} hours at the same speed. How many km will {a.he} go tomorrow?
exercise: How many km does a car travel in {h} hours at {s} km an hour?
