exercise: {a}'s family drives across Texas at {s} km an hour for {h.words} hours. How many km do they drive?
exercise: A ferry in New Zealand sails {s} km every hour. How far does it sail in {h} hours?
exercise: A truck covered {s*g} km in {g} hours. If it keeps the same speed, how many km will it cover in {h} hours?
exercise: A motorbike goes {s} km in each hour. What distance does it go in {h} hours?
test: For {h} hours a car in Queensland keeps a steady speed of {s} km an hour. What distance does it cover?
test: {a} drove from Dublin for {g} hours and travelled {s*g} km. How far would {a.he} travel in {h} hours at the same speed?
test: What distance in km is covered in {h} hours by a bus going {s} km each hour?
test: A camper van in Scotland travels at {s} km per hour. How many km does it travel in {h} hours?
test: A lorry needs {g} hours for {s*g} km. Driving just as fast, how many km does it do in {h} hours?
test: Going at {s} km an hour, {a} rides in a car for {h} hours. How many km long is the trip?
